From: Mostafa Saleh <smostafa@google.com>
Date: Wed Apr 9 09:43:32 2025 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: iommu: Restrict access KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID

KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID should only mirror the host stage-2,
without interaction with pv interface.

Bug: 277989609
Bug: 278749606
Change-Id: I6d9800c1a12c9f4dbfbb51c22f589614424aabaa
Signed-off-by: Mostafa Saleh <smostafa@google.com>

[gki6677 reshape note - 2026-11-02, Z.ai]
Reshaped for the 6.6.77 pin (deprecated/android15-6.6-2025-03 @
8d05d8f2439f) as recorded in the B-2 triage: (1) the map-guard
returns 0 instead of upstream's -EINVAL - at the pin
kvm_iommu_map_pages() returns the size_t mapped count, so -EINVAL
would read back as a huge count (same pin-contract reasoning as
Batch A 0003); (2) the map/unmap hunks re-anchor after the
IS_ALIGNED guards shipped in Batch A 0003 (upstream order overflow
-> IS_ALIGNED -> IDMAP guard preserved). The unmap and
iova_to_phys guards are verbatim, and the resulting post-state is
byte-identical to upstream modulo the documented map-guard error
code. Upstream's own error-code conversion (2a89c059adae,
"iommu: Return map error code") is deliberately not shipped - see
the B-2 skip list. Verified: strict git apply on the pin replica
+ guard-by-guard compare vs the upstream post-state.

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 1a45ce72b0cfc24e01d278723754ecdb23de2c15
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class B, RESHAPED for the pin; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
index 978e86cbc..cfcbeea33 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
@@ -500,6 +500,9 @@ size_t kvm_iommu_map_pages(pkvm_handle_t domain_id, unsigned long iova,
 	if (!IS_ALIGNED(iova | paddr, pgsize))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (domain_id == KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID)
+		return 0;
+
 	domain = handle_to_domain(domain_id);
 	if (!domain || domain_get(domain))
 		return 0;
@@ -599,6 +602,9 @@ size_t kvm_iommu_unmap_pages(pkvm_handle_t domain_id,
 	if (!IS_ALIGNED(iova, pgsize))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (domain_id == KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID)
+		return 0;
+
 	domain = handle_to_domain(domain_id);
 	if (!domain || domain_get(domain))
 		return 0;
@@ -630,6 +636,9 @@ phys_addr_t kvm_iommu_iova_to_phys(pkvm_handle_t domain_id, unsigned long iova)
 	if (!kvm_iommu_ops || !kvm_iommu_ops->iova_to_phys)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (domain_id == KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID)
+		return iova;
+
 	domain = handle_to_domain( domain_id);
 
 	if (!domain || domain_get(domain))
